  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14131900/assets/0269db77d9a551b6f75e260bac9d3385d6cfad05d15359bff6f059e0050ef1dc.png)\n\nFirst, notice that $∠ROS$ and $∠SOT$ are adjacent because they share the same side $\\overset{\\to }{OS}.$\n\nWe can add the measures of two adjacent angles to find the measure of the combined angle.\n\nTherefore: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠ROT & =m∠ROS+m∠SOT \\\\  & ={55}^{∘}+{66}^{∘} \\\\  & ={121}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
